window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>Roman</b></p> <p>At twelve years old, Roman Covington—crown prince of the tropical fae kingdom—met Violet Maekin: a girl with freckles on her nose, a razor-edged wit, and the ability to make him laugh. She made him feel normal in a world that demanded he be anything but. After just a single day and a few scribbled notes, she held his heart in her hands.</p> <p>But when Roman turned thirteen, the gods granted him the name of his fated mate—Vivian. Violet's identical twin sister.</p> <p>Convinced the gods were cruel, mistaken, or both, Roman spent a decade seeking a way to shift the bond from one sister to the other. All the while, a quiet madness bloomed within him.</p> <p>He watched Violet from the shadows.</p> <p>Stalked her in silence.</p> <p>Killed for her in the dark.</p> <p><b>Violet</b></p> <p>When the king and queen arrived to announce the prince's gods-blessed mate, Violet already knew it was her.</p> <p>Except it wasn't.</p> <p>Vivian got Roman, and Violet got nothing but a splintered heart and the cruel ache of pretending it didn't break her.</p> <p>But Violet and Roman's friendship endured…until the day she realized her feelings had grown into something vast and soul-deep, far beyond the reaches of her childhood crush.</p> <p>Roman and Vivian might avoid one another now, but Violet knew the gods did not make mistakes. Their indifference would turn to love while Violet's heart would turn to ash.</p> <p>She did the only thing she could to save her heart and walked away from Roman for good.</p> <p>Obsessively Yours <i>is a dual POV romance book in a classic fantasy setting, but there is minimal world-building and no fantasy plot unrelated to the romance. No cheating and a guaranteed HEA. It is book two in a series of interconnected standalones that may be enjoyed in any order.</i></p> <p><i>Tropes include: childhood friends to star-crossed lovers, fated mates, stalking, morally black MMC, virgin hero, possessive/jealous hero, found family humor, animal familiars, OWD, touch her and die (literally).</i></p> <p><i>Contains mature content. A complete list of content warnings can be found on the author's website. Narrated in duet style.</i></p>"; 
